<p>{{ site.name }} is an independent Formula 1 news site for fans in the United States. We cover the news, the driver market, the teams, results, standings and the rules, and we convert every session time to Eastern, Central, Mountain and Pacific time. We keep hubs for the three American races, <a href="{{ '/hubs/las-vegas/' | url }}">Las Vegas</a>, <a href="{{ '/hubs/miami/' | url }}">Miami</a> and <a href="{{ '/hubs/austin/' | url }}">Austin</a>, and for <a href="{{ '/hubs/cadillac/' | url }}">Cadillac</a>, the American team. Stories carry the byline {{ site.author }}.</p>
<p>{{ site.disclaimerLine }}</p>
<h2>How a story earns a place on the site</h2>
<p>Every published story lists its sources with a title, a public URL, the publisher and a date, and the claims in the story link to those pages. The build fails if a story has no source list. Results and points are checked against the official classification. Rumor is labeled as rumor and attributed to the outlet that reported it.</p>
<p>We do not invent quotes, results, times or events. If a fact is not in a source, it does not go in the story.</p>
<h2>Standards</h2>
<p>The publishing rules are on <a href="{{ '/sources-ethics/' | url }}">Sources &amp; Ethics</a>. A factual error is corrected on the article; how to send one is on <a href="{{ '/corrections/' | url }}">Corrections</a>. We do not publish a street address.</p>
